#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147172 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06fedec8-5aed-52f9-bd4f-aa81b9180ad4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems With Sinusoidal Forcing"}] :question/id #uuid "abd7efc4-f397-564d-a471-17b1ffc93fb3" :question/math-academy-id "e-21862" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t} - 2y = -5\\sin t, \\qquad y(0)=1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal L\\{\\sin\\omega t\\} = \\dfrac{\\omega}{s^2+\\omega^2}, \\qquad \\mathcal L\\{\\cos\\omega t\\} = \\dfrac{s}{s^2+\\omega^2}, \\qquad s > 0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s) = \\mathcal L \\{y(t)\\}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/assets/476c6ff72b2927d4d86291e5b9816e54f9c7b3fd254b4f8d73de493162a4a4b7.png)\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/assets/8c16e1eed467dbc46fb8698f9a7e2ceff80d47e571506806fe1baf37ec1050ed.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/assets/a728d0243548e724f95b2331697d75972e05774cf9b9a708c0965361d5e75fc8.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\{y'\\} - 2\\mathcal{L}\\{y\\} = -5\\mathcal{L}\\{\\sin t\\}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $\\mathcal{L}\\{y'\\} = sY(s) - y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transform\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\{\\sin t\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s^2+1},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-1)-2Y(s) & =-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s)-1 & =-\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, add $1$ to the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-2)Y(s) & =1-\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{2}+1}-\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s-2),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s) =\\dfrac{s^2 - 4}{(s - 2)(s^2 + 1)} = \\dfrac{(s-2)(s+2)}{(s - 2)(s^2 + 1)} = \\dfrac{s+2}{s^2 + 1}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}}+2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147303 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1417a42-f47a-5611-84be-f331c75287a9" :knowledge-point/title "Laplace Transforms of First-Order Linear IVPs"}] :question/id #uuid "700f5e8f-33f6-568a-ad11-d2664336725d" :question/math-academy-id "e-6657" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s) = \\mathcal L\\{y(t)\\}$ for $s > 1$ if \n\n$$\ny' + y =  2e^t, \\qquad y(0)=-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}+y} & =L{2{e}^{t}} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}+L{y} & =2L{{e}^{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $\\mathcal L\\left\\{ y' \\right\\},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=-1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y'\\right\\}  = sY(s) - y(0)   = sY(s) + 1\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal L \\{e^{at}\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s-a}, \\qquad s > a\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following result:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L} \\{ e^t \\}  = \\dfrac{1}{s-1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}+L{y} & =2L{{e}^{t}} \\\\ (sY(s)+1)+Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{s-1} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{s-1}-1 \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2-(s-1)}{s-1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{3-s}{{s}^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147304 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eae6b5d-adff-53b2-970d-f0dcee58365f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Laplace Transforms"}] :question/id #uuid "409c5aa3-5c53-5ab4-b2f7-bcfe01a14914" :question/math-academy-id "e-6661" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t} + 4y = 3e^{-t}, \\qquad y(0)=2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms.\n\nLet $Y(s) = \\mathcal L \\{y(t)\\}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/assets/1da481c39504266a4f42e13ef938ff0f7eb75d1174a149bed8d80e47e25d46e6.png)\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/assets/ffa301a263d519d3b653c1e1be9b8e8ef59f3cb2fb515e794c00b6b27dadc762.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/assets/54fb8d20b3cd1205ec6ee7c94b74418e45bc239229159c093dbb34bd908f72fd.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\{y'\\} + 4\\mathcal{L}\\{y\\} = 3\\mathcal{L}\\{e^{-t}\\}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative, $\\mathcal{L}\\{y'\\} = sY(s) - y(0),$ and the standard transform \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\{e^{at}\\} = \\frac{1}{s-a}, \\qquad s > a,\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-2)+4Y(s) & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+1} \\\\ (s+4)Y(s)-2 & =\\frac{3}{s+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, add $2$ to the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+4)Y(s) & =2+\\frac{3}{s+1} \\\\ (s+4)Y(s) & =\\frac{2(s+1)}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s+1} \\\\ (s+4)Y(s) & =\\frac{2s+5}{s+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+4),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s) =\\dfrac{2s+5}{(s + 4)(s+1)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. We write $Y(s)$ in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2s+5}{(s+4)(s+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{s+4} + \\dfrac{B}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants $A$ and $B,$ we first clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n2s+5 = A(s+1) + B(s+4)\n$$\n\nNow, we find the constants $A$ and $B.$\n\n- Setting $s = -4,$ we have\n\n$$\n2(-4)+5 = A(-4+1) + B(0) \\implies -3 = -3A \\implies A = 1.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s = -1,$ we have\n\n$$\n2(-1)+5 = A(0) + B(-1+4) \\implies 3 = 3B \\implies B = 1.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s) = \\dfrac{1}{s+4} + \\dfrac{1}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+4}} & ={e}^{-4t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} & ={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+4}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} \\\\ y(t) & ={e}^{-4t}+{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1417a42-f47a-5611-84be-f331c75287a9" :knowledge-point/title "Laplace Transforms of First-Order Linear IVPs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1ae5660-cc3b-51f5-aca8-bb968f9d26b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s-9}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376256} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e38a32-aa05-5f79-8892-51b357b4c656" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376257} {:answer/id #uuid "b59f2167-cb9b-50e0-995d-e1740cb41e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s-9}{{s}^{2}-9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376258} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f65c39-da30-50e6-9fa4-2eed0a90465a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376259} {:answer/id #uuid "546d319e-b90c-5d52-a99e-42e555a43a83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s+9}{{s}^{2}-9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b59f2167-cb9b-50e0-995d-e1740cb41e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s-9}{{s}^{2}-9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376258} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa5e86f9-4acc-50bb-a684-a4e69ad551c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "68891c85-8075-57df-acec-5850a69663ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-342473" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>3$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+y=-8\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t,\\,y(0)=1.\n$$\n\nYou may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>|\\omega |.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}+y} & =L{-8\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}+L{y} & =-8L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=1:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sL{y}-y(0)=sY(s)-1\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9},\\,s>3\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}+L{y} & =-8L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t} \\\\ (sY(s)-1)+Y(s) & =-8(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}) \\\\ sY(s)+Y(s) & =1-\\frac{8s}{{s}^{2}-9} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-8s-9}{{s}^{2}-9} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-8s-9}{({s}^{2}-9)(s+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s>3,$ we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y(s) & =\\frac{({s}^{2}-8s-9)}{({s}^{2}-9)(s+1)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{(s-9)(s+1)}{({s}^{2}-9)(s+1)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{s-9}{{s}^{2}-9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eae6b5d-adff-53b2-970d-f0dcee58365f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d82507e-cfd4-5c70-8253-d38c28c3b66f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{(s-5)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376263} {:answer/id #uuid "16cc6f65-d95e-51fc-8020-f6a8851828de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376264} {:answer/id #uuid "b5fad86a-f336-50f9-aa55-69c947778b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{(s-3)(s+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376265} {:answer/id #uuid "f0c76abd-2ff9-506d-a662-41eee89b0af1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(s-9)(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376266} {:answer/id #uuid "7080d319-d36f-5394-8eec-db1fe7d73ea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(s-3)(s+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16cc6f65-d95e-51fc-8020-f6a8851828de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376264} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a51e059-6b87-5a34-aa48-c82b7b72c38c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adf17116-05f3-5625-8869-7d1f9134b23a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4(s-3)}-\\frac{9}{4(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376269} {:answer/id #uuid "84bc0f96-2c54-5a4b-93c8-6a0e25f205ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{4(s-3)}+\\frac{9}{4(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376270} {:answer/id #uuid "992abd36-e96f-5a75-baca-baba1087b483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8(s-3)}-\\frac{9}{8(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376271} {:answer/id #uuid "51c18268-1e76-551e-8b3b-10bab078134e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{8(s-3)}+\\frac{9}{8(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "992abd36-e96f-5a75-baca-baba1087b483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8(s-3)}-\\frac{9}{8(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376271} :answer-field/id #uuid "edc9dd91-8200-590a-b85c-d6b7695c41db" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376268} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9246a9de-6158-532d-9e69-302541aa845e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376274} {:answer/id #uuid "17621032-b8b2-51bd-a757-861960e83a04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{3t}+\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376275} {:answer/id #uuid "927b4f87-2f3b-5f08-a7fd-79f03026c778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-3t}+\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376276} {:answer/id #uuid "d19f32dc-bee3-5872-bf86-62812ad6669a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-3t}-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9246a9de-6158-532d-9e69-302541aa845e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376274} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce562a5b-66d9-54ee-931c-8a87cff182fc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31e8084f-ab1a-5236-ac36-9b6a9937b2ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-342499" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+5y=9{e}^{3t},\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms.\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+5L{y}=L{9{e}^{3t}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative, $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0),$ and the standard transform \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\,s>a,\n$$\n\n \nwe substitute the known values.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sY(s)-0+5Y(s) & =9\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-3} \\\\ (s+5)Y(s) & =\\frac{9}{s-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $Y(s),$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. We write $Y(s)$ in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}=\\frac{A}{s-3}+\\frac{B}{s+5}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants $A$ and $B,$ we first clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n9=A(s+5)+B(s-3)\n$$\n\nNow, we find the constants $A$ and $B.$\n\n- Setting $s=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n9=A(3+5)+B(0)\\,⟹\\,9=8A\\,⟹\\,A=\\frac{9}{8}.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-5,$ we have\n\n$$\n9=A(0)+B(-5-3)\\,⟹\\,9=-8B\\,⟹\\,B=-\\frac{9}{8}.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{9}{8(s-3)}-\\frac{9}{8(s+5)}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-3}} & ={e}^{3t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+5}} & ={e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =\\frac{9}{8}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-3}}-\\frac{9}{8}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+5}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eae6b5d-adff-53b2-970d-f0dcee58365f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6869da3f-f11d-5bb2-adca-fc09ccd32806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(s-1)(s+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376280} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a90e27-17a9-5fe4-923d-e2100d8a3b60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(s-1)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376281} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a9c87e-02fc-5276-8d1c-31c785c54322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(s-4)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376282} {:answer/id #uuid "a977ae90-62c6-54a1-ae8e-3b10ef153091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(s-4)(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376283} {:answer/id #uuid "be9a8979-1ab7-5d49-ace6-6aebed7101f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(s-3)(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5a90e27-17a9-5fe4-923d-e2100d8a3b60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(s-1)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376281} :answer-field/id #uuid "de72a231-c50c-5cf5-b512-de6e478b009e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376279} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4ceff24-c828-5a41-8ce4-fe47ccd8b4b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376286} {:answer/id #uuid "5a2b8f35-a769-5e82-bd6c-9ba3503c20c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376287} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f70107-2e50-5540-8a5f-3a5a19f38e9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s-1}-\\frac{2}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376288} {:answer/id #uuid "49d35240-ae76-5ec3-a553-6f448c528336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49d35240-ae76-5ec3-a553-6f448c528336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376289} :answer-field/id #uuid "da1d6e3a-5c1a-589e-955a-14b182a69341" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376285} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "435e3789-586d-5ba7-9440-d5cd2b83aae7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{-t}+{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376291} {:answer/id #uuid "41adf22a-e739-5846-84a4-1e466d05e62f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{t}+{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376292} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f73324-b7af-53c5-94b7-0f668e00a131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-t}-{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376293} {:answer/id #uuid "01061cf2-5097-5d05-b4dc-4910c8b171cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}-{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01061cf2-5097-5d05-b4dc-4910c8b171cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}-{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376294} :answer-field/id #uuid "83094b09-cfcb-5a40-82e0-b98be7510e59" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376290}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb48c3d2-004e-5e70-aa77-14e4f91382fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-342501" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+3y=4{e}^{t},\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms.\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+3L{y}=L{4{e}^{t}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative, $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0),$ and the standard transform \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\,s>a,\n$$\n\n \nwe substitute the known values.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sY(s)-0+3Y(s) & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-1} \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{4}{s-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $Y(s),$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{4}{(s-1)(s+3)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. We write $Y(s)$ in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{(s-1)(s+3)}=\\frac{A}{s-1}+\\frac{B}{s+3}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants $A$ and $B,$ we first clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n4=A(s+3)+B(s-1)\n$$\n\nNow, we find the constants $A$ and $B.$\n\n- Setting $s=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n4=A(1+3)+B(0)\\,⟹\\,4=4A\\,⟹\\,A=1.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n4=A(0)+B(-3-1)\\,⟹\\,4=-4B\\,⟹\\,B=-1.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s+3}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}} & ={e}^{t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} & ={e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} \\\\ y(t) & ={e}^{t}-{e}^{-3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eae6b5d-adff-53b2-970d-f0dcee58365f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eda4638b-0eb4-500a-abb3-ffc275469746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376297} {:answer/id #uuid "2ebfb6d4-a39f-5714-a5c8-e1938b3dbf38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s-2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376298} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb7aa20-fb14-5fc5-aedc-da5bd932c547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s+4}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376299} {:answer/id #uuid "998d2bcc-ba6a-5458-bc5d-692ff6791ee0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s+2}{s(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376300} {:answer/id #uuid "66b5116a-464e-5ebb-9cab-4afe1ef827c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eda4638b-0eb4-500a-abb3-ffc275469746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376297} :answer-field/id #uuid "274fc8d2-782a-5024-983d-e20fde8913f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376296} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ceb536c-af2a-5733-aa89-33d31f41d043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376303} {:answer/id #uuid "f84810bb-a1cb-5bca-89bf-2b7678841ef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376304} {:answer/id #uuid "d4839c07-cb11-58d4-b28a-1c0fc35cd480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376305} {:answer/id #uuid "e3f6c690-07f6-5cc7-9229-33ed27b800be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3f6c690-07f6-5cc7-9229-33ed27b800be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376306} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4b06d87-21f0-5470-8f76-ab6711ec1654" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376302} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad8f6370-8926-51c3-877b-2c275ff205ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+2t-2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376308} {:answer/id #uuid "368bc71a-ac61-5108-86ca-46292a3edf9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2-2t+2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376309} {:answer/id #uuid "4d793fa5-cf85-55c1-809e-08e740d79dd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2+2t+2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376310} {:answer/id #uuid "da512dee-b596-5e6e-a005-18649513d49e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-2t-2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad8f6370-8926-51c3-877b-2c275ff205ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+2t-2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376308} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6baf80b-c422-5111-9969-8b5b6343774d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d4a5a1a-5811-5a7d-99a0-f3fb86ea4705" :question/math-academy-id "q-342704" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y=2t+4,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+L{y}=2L{t}+4L{1}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard polynomial transforms\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{t} & =\\frac{1!}{{s}^{1+1}}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}, \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{0!}{{s}^{0+1}}=\\frac{1}{s},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-0)+Y(s) & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{4}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{4s}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+1)$ and a repeated linear factor ${s}^{2},$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}=\\frac{A}{s}+\\frac{B}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n4s+2=As(s+1)+B(s+1)+C{s}^{2}\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-1,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n4(-1)+2=A(0)+B(0)+C(-1)^{2}\\,⟹\\,-2=C\\,⟹\\,C=-2.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=0,$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n4(0)+2=A(0)+B(0+1)+C(0)\\,⟹\\,2=B\\,⟹\\,B=2.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of $s,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n4=A+B\\,⟹\\,4=A+2\\,⟹\\,A=2.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} & =1 \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}} & =t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} & ={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}}-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} \\\\ y(t) & =2+2t-2{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1417a42-f47a-5611-84be-f331c75287a9" :knowledge-point/title "Laplace Transforms of First-Order Linear IVPs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb5658fd-46fe-5fcb-99a4-8688e6af657a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376314} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce1e423-ed56-56b7-8e70-db0ba70db09a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s+2}{({s}^{2}+1)(s-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376315} {:answer/id #uuid "01f868dd-ab7d-545c-9d3f-2aafc72bfe86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s-2}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376316} {:answer/id #uuid "2777dd67-f9cf-594b-8bfb-ed1af76d7797" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s+2}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376317} {:answer/id #uuid "0b62bfad-3067-590d-b150-9cf0b4711145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2777dd67-f9cf-594b-8bfb-ed1af76d7797" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s+2}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376317} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ac1d161-04fb-5d09-ba47-f01cbbfa805a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376313}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8a59cf6b-30d9-5a4e-b2af-691e5237e06b" :question/math-academy-id "q-342871" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>2$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-2y=-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y(0)=1.\n$$\n\nYou may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}-2y} & =L{-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =-5L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=1:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sL{y}-y(0)=sY(s)-1\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,s>0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =-5L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\ (sY(s)-1)-2Y(s) & =-5(\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}) \\\\ sY(s)-2Y(s) & =1-\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{({s}^{2}+1)(s-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s>2,$ we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y(s) & =\\frac{(s-2)(s+2)}{({s}^{2}+1)(s-2)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eae6b5d-adff-53b2-970d-f0dcee58365f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c2b75a1-e945-52df-bccf-124561b85ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s+5}{(s+2)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376321} {:answer/id #uuid "05859868-a2d2-5839-814c-425e75ffd3a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(s+2)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376322} {:answer/id #uuid "d13bd291-c482-5340-a0e0-d0d148b79fb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s+8}{(s+2)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376323} {:answer/id #uuid "14fc84a2-ef56-5cee-9bb5-49dc9d9a456e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{(s+2)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376324} {:answer/id #uuid "2d283d4a-71fa-5e77-b0d4-c0481b83d836" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{(s+2)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d13bd291-c482-5340-a0e0-d0d148b79fb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s+8}{(s+2)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376323} :answer-field/id #uuid "18a28960-3a2f-5c96-993b-ca240445f345" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10d56cc4-5ff9-537b-8dfe-e69861f8abb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{s+2}+\\frac{5}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376327} {:answer/id #uuid "1ba95dfb-6926-5c2e-97b0-fbf26fc6b709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{s+2}-\\frac{5}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376328} {:answer/id #uuid "196588cb-45c6-5956-90c6-1e45e65d978d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+2}+\\frac{1}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376329} {:answer/id #uuid "fedbec1e-c12f-582e-af86-541d65fb7f46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{s+2}-\\frac{6}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ba95dfb-6926-5c2e-97b0-fbf26fc6b709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{s+2}-\\frac{5}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376328} :answer-field/id #uuid "22a81cf4-1dce-5481-8b59-f895c6252b68" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376326} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f126cff3-2477-53fa-85a0-8ae16b664294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{e}^{-2t}+5{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376332} {:answer/id #uuid "6e2deca0-7317-5a15-8ab9-5dc2fdd44688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2t}+{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376333} {:answer/id #uuid "baac865f-2c57-54a6-9128-787ee4d327a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{e}^{-2t}-6{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376334} {:answer/id #uuid "e0c1b5d2-c003-5d45-8add-3ec38941400e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{e}^{-2t}-5{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0c1b5d2-c003-5d45-8add-3ec38941400e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{e}^{-2t}-5{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376335} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bfc881c-a9ca-57ab-8976-6bcc0476ad03" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5a07952f-1818-5784-8ecb-b69e9feaafac" :question/math-academy-id "q-342925" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+2y=5{e}^{-3t},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms.\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+2L{y}=L{5{e}^{-3t}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative, $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0),$ and the standard transform \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\,s>a,\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-1)+2Y(s) & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+3} \\\\ (s+2)Y(s)-1 & =\\frac{5}{s+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, add $1$ to the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+2)Y(s) & =1+\\frac{5}{s+3} \\\\ (s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{s+3}{s+3}+\\frac{5}{s+3} \\\\ (s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{s+8}{s+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+2),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{s+8}{(s+2)(s+3)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. We write $Y(s)$ in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{s+8}{(s+2)(s+3)}=\\frac{A}{s+2}+\\frac{B}{s+3}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants $A$ and $B,$ we first clear the denominators:\n\n$$\ns+8=A(s+3)+B(s+2)\n$$\n\nNow, we find the constants $A$ and $B.$\n\n- Setting $s=-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n-2+8=A(-2+3)+B(0)\\,⟹\\,6=1A\\,⟹\\,A=6.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n-3+8=A(0)+B(-3+2)\\,⟹\\,5=-1B\\,⟹\\,B=-5.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{6}{s+2}-\\frac{5}{s+3}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} & ={e}^{-2t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} & ={e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =6{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}-5{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} \\\\ y(t) & =6{e}^{-2t}-5{e}^{-3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eae6b5d-adff-53b2-970d-f0dcee58365f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6017f00-685d-543b-b09e-60738602220e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s}{(s+3)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376338} {:answer/id #uuid "db7057ce-f702-51f2-b075-141dad40ffcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(s+3)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376339} {:answer/id #uuid "4ed51709-652b-5c4d-8441-c56578271117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s+4}{(s+3)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376340} {:answer/id #uuid "8f71dcbd-62b0-5322-9abc-cd2714975b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(s+3)(s-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376341} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6e7ff3-c99b-5237-b7c8-e95361ba1132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s+8}{(s+3)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb6e7ff3-c99b-5237-b7c8-e95361ba1132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s+8}{(s+3)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376342} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca29b225-eb90-59eb-8feb-a9214996a27d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3cd82b0-87d3-58e5-a2cd-eb9bdcdde6d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+3}+\\frac{1}{s+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376344} {:answer/id #uuid "a27f9f4b-895c-5a54-a319-9dbd48080857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s+3}-\\frac{4}{s+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376345} {:answer/id #uuid "f8df5f9d-c42e-570f-a9f5-5daf77c75f06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{s+3}+\\frac{2}{s+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376346} {:answer/id #uuid "74eb85d5-448e-5ada-af6f-6ff9654c27b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{s+3}+\\frac{4}{s+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74eb85d5-448e-5ada-af6f-6ff9654c27b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{s+3}+\\frac{4}{s+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376347} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3c0cc10-5b6d-5b98-9136-c46279a8b54d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376343} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b143573-25c8-5dc9-a5bc-2fa042c7704b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-3t}+4{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376349} {:answer/id #uuid "ab0f8cc3-76bb-5ba3-a526-637c5f27f87f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3t}+{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376350} {:answer/id #uuid "99fc16a3-25f9-5cca-a30e-3705f047d832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{e}^{-3t}+2{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376351} {:answer/id #uuid "109cb8f4-4edb-5650-8468-dddbe422fcfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-3t}-4{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b143573-25c8-5dc9-a5bc-2fa042c7704b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-3t}+4{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376349} :answer-field/id #uuid "91904cd2-3308-58bc-ba42-af2bd9d1c9b0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1bebe255-48b8-5821-81d8-8df520eed6e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-342928" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+3y=4{e}^{-2t},\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms.\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+3L{y}=L{4{e}^{-2t}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative, $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0),$ and the standard transform \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\,s>a,\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-2)+3Y(s) & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+2} \\\\ (s+3)Y(s)-2 & =\\frac{4}{s+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, add $2$ to the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+3)Y(s) & =2+\\frac{4}{s+2} \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{2(s+2)}{s+2}+\\frac{4}{s+2} \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{2s+8}{s+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{2s+8}{(s+3)(s+2)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. We write $Y(s)$ in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{2s+8}{(s+3)(s+2)}=\\frac{A}{s+3}+\\frac{B}{s+2}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants $A$ and $B,$ we first clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n2s+8=A(s+2)+B(s+3)\n$$\n\nNow, we find the constants $A$ and $B.$\n\n- Setting $s=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n2(-3)+8=A(-3+2)+B(0)\\,⟹\\,2=-1A\\,⟹\\,A=-2.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n2(-2)+8=A(0)+B(-2+3)\\,⟹\\,4=1B\\,⟹\\,B=4.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=-\\frac{2}{s+3}+\\frac{4}{s+2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} & ={e}^{-3t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} & ={e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}}+4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} \\\\ y(t) & =-2{e}^{-3t}+4{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06fedec8-5aed-52f9-bd4f-aa81b9180ad4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems With Sinusoidal Forcing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42c3c56b-d6ba-5058-b4f5-b733df1d8828" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s-4}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376355} {:answer/id #uuid "94904768-c30d-5d98-bca3-086bbf42d7c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s+4}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376356} {:answer/id #uuid "62d0f9da-2a55-575c-a31d-351ec5153325" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376357} {:answer/id #uuid "e90f7175-17f3-5380-812d-b266097618ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376358} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e6048c-679a-52d5-a3b2-a525ba56b7a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4-s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2e6048c-679a-52d5-a3b2-a525ba56b7a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4-s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376359} :answer-field/id #uuid "4efd81cd-3cef-5c44-ba2f-f0e48a4a6f46" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376354} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a4e0470-c113-5ebe-9e66-32bb0e51aed1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s+2}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376361} {:answer/id #uuid "62b9cfce-8628-5c76-b977-1cffe7babb3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10(s+2)}-\\frac{3s+4}{10({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376362} {:answer/id #uuid "d43c601c-7af0-53a6-9cd2-e215933394fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+2}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376363} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc8670b-e14d-5141-9473-843e7ea4e6ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10(s+2)}+\\frac{3s+4}{10({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62b9cfce-8628-5c76-b977-1cffe7babb3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10(s+2)}-\\frac{3s+4}{10({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376362} :answer-field/id #uuid "a520ff57-88e6-5e9f-87ed-f1587f9df143" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376360} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66fd85df-5d7d-5477-ae5f-1711c169e460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}+\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376366} {:answer/id #uuid "f3d2e46e-dbf3-5db8-a56b-cff411b52180" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376367} {:answer/id #uuid "60407bcf-2bd2-5a9d-9754-cba8d17d6550" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}-\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376368} {:answer/id #uuid "63030385-ff8e-51e6-a1cb-fe62adcd0514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}-\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60407bcf-2bd2-5a9d-9754-cba8d17d6550" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}-\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376368} :answer-field/id #uuid "274d1f01-5a5a-556d-ae0c-af145b61fc53" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1873e66d-b721-525d-8ac0-7b13c3d92c58" :question/math-academy-id "q-342960" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+2y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+2L{y}=L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t}-L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t}=\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-0)+2Y(s) & =\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16} \\\\ (s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{4-s}{{s}^{2}+16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ Dividing by $(s+2),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{4-s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+2)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+16),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}=\\frac{A}{s+2}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+16}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n4-s=A({s}^{2}+16)+(Bs+C)(s+2)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-2,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n4-(-2)=A((-2)^{2}+16)+0\\,⟹\\,6=20A\\,⟹\\,A=\\frac{3}{10}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n0=A+B\\,⟹\\,0=\\frac{3}{10}+B\\,⟹\\,B=-\\frac{3}{10}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n4=16A+2C\\,⟹\\,4=\\frac{48}{10}+2C\\,⟹\\,C=-\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{3}{10(s+2)}+\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{10}s-\\frac{2}{5})}{{s}^{2}+16}=\\frac{3}{10(s+2)}-\\frac{3s+4}{10({s}^{2}+16)}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} & ={e}^{-2t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =\\frac{3}{10}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}-\\frac{3}{10}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}}-\\frac{1}{10}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}-\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06fedec8-5aed-52f9-bd4f-aa81b9180ad4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems With Sinusoidal Forcing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7da514e5-20be-57aa-8353-8795fb167de3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s+1}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376372} {:answer/id #uuid "fbd6831c-9723-5189-8d55-ec7ddaa56480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376373} {:answer/id #uuid "3406b875-3771-5b64-a5d5-f6d0c182a580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376374} {:answer/id #uuid "9526f984-319a-5b30-b137-df0bc184474d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s-1}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376375} {:answer/id #uuid "9041cf93-3f7b-5d45-b35f-94a5dc3802e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7da514e5-20be-57aa-8353-8795fb167de3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s+1}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376372} :answer-field/id #uuid "04a3b383-50ec-5653-a75d-a3bbf3234f21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fed2cf55-5bf3-5a8d-9a87-5a8e5d04ab1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5(s+2)}+\\frac{s+3}{5({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376378} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7a7893-4b3d-5af3-8a9f-80db8659aea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+2}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376379} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6ded10-9636-5a49-a499-bbc11b88d601" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5(s+2)}-\\frac{s+3}{5({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376380} {:answer/id #uuid "369918db-e74f-555b-9cfc-2fb171c2bb1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5(s+2)}-\\frac{s+3}{5({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fed2cf55-5bf3-5a8d-9a87-5a8e5d04ab1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5(s+2)}+\\frac{s+3}{5({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376378} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2e5dbec-32f7-5b53-86ba-967e78e52d8f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376377} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "426e0ed9-fb00-5187-af01-055481dc101f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-2t}+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376383} {:answer/id #uuid "f215cf7f-6c28-525f-afc7-76a650078933" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-2t}-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376384} {:answer/id #uuid "cf1ffbe0-3544-5a06-9a10-26f88b352650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-2t}-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376385} {:answer/id #uuid "44bc25aa-e3f7-5436-9b6f-f8d1e3a0fa51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "426e0ed9-fb00-5187-af01-055481dc101f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-2t}+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376383} :answer-field/id #uuid "32df38cd-b4dd-56f9-857a-82a5d314d067" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2839b85c-1838-5d26-90a6-4ced0d0fbb59" :question/math-academy-id "q-342961" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+2y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+2L{y}=L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-0)+2Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ Dividing by $(s+2),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{s+1}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+1)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+2)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+1),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{s+1}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+1)}=\\frac{A}{s+2}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\ns+1=A({s}^{2}+1)+(Bs+C)(s+2)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-2,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n-2+1=A((-2)^{2}+1)+0\\,⟹\\,-1=5A\\,⟹\\,A=-\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n0=A+B\\,⟹\\,0=-\\frac{1}{5}+B\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n1=A+2C\\,⟹\\,1=-\\frac{1}{5}+2C\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{5})}{s+2}+\\frac{(\\frac{1}{5}s+\\frac{3}{5})}{{s}^{2}+1}=-\\frac{1}{5(s+2)}+\\frac{s+3}{5({s}^{2}+1)}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} & ={e}^{-2t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =-\\frac{1}{5}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}+\\frac{1}{5}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}}+\\frac{3}{5}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} \\\\ y(t) & =-\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-2t}+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376387 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06fedec8-5aed-52f9-bd4f-aa81b9180ad4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems With Sinusoidal Forcing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86792d2b-60ff-537b-ab67-ac4402ecb5cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376389} {:answer/id #uuid "e7319b6f-eaad-59d1-be37-2283ecdb9052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3-s}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376390} {:answer/id #uuid "f71b6b84-c584-5ef9-a3bb-2245971c7048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s-3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376391} {:answer/id #uuid "43cf1c2a-b07a-51d7-96fd-ac41c715fbe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s+3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376392} {:answer/id #uuid "7544bdef-51a1-55a0-aa85-8c31da6353b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43cf1c2a-b07a-51d7-96fd-ac41c715fbe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s+3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376392} :answer-field/id #uuid "39f97f40-d834-5573-807b-7a3920414f87" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376388} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c844a248-4740-5331-83df-7ddc848fc4d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15(s+6)}-\\frac{s+9}{15({s}^{2}+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376395} {:answer/id #uuid "536d4958-cfa8-5279-8e74-222ad17a166a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15(s+6)}+\\frac{s+9}{15({s}^{2}+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376396} {:answer/id #uuid "d96406b6-7886-5b20-b01e-59590c6549d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15(s+6)}-\\frac{s+9}{15({s}^{2}+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376397} {:answer/id #uuid "546b6eca-0c52-596f-b86d-2a00fc3cb10e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+6}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "536d4958-cfa8-5279-8e74-222ad17a166a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15(s+6)}+\\frac{s+9}{15({s}^{2}+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376396} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b371c09-1b84-5c40-a240-3336bafbae33" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d10e5897-d51d-5566-a824-444b8fb7a7a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15}{e}^{-6t}-\\frac{1}{15}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376400} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5e7db2-5f33-5442-b570-67b23362de91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}{e}^{-6t}-\\frac{1}{15}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376401} {:answer/id #uuid "1e424a2b-53c7-50b4-a3a6-d51b4a1381ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15}{e}^{-6t}+\\frac{1}{15}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376402} {:answer/id #uuid "4501155a-4863-57de-a6c0-fb1a9373e798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-6t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e424a2b-53c7-50b4-a3a6-d51b4a1381ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15}{e}^{-6t}+\\frac{1}{15}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376402} :answer-field/id #uuid "435efd9b-b860-5744-8489-57d886c5daa0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe117573-5606-5478-b552-48739b413505" :question/math-academy-id "q-342962" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+6y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+6L{y}=L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}+L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}=\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-0)+6Y(s) & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9} \\\\ (s+6)Y(s) & =\\frac{s+3}{{s}^{2}+9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ Dividing by $(s+6),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{s+3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+6)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+9),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{s+3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}=\\frac{A}{s+6}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+9}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\ns+3=A({s}^{2}+9)+(Bs+C)(s+6)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-6,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n-6+3=A((-6)^{2}+9)+0\\,⟹\\,-3=45A\\,⟹\\,A=-\\frac{1}{15}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n0=A+B\\,⟹\\,0=-\\frac{1}{15}+B\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{1}{15}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n3=9A+6C\\,⟹\\,3=-\\frac{3}{5}+6C\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{15})}{s+6}+\\frac{(\\frac{1}{15}s+\\frac{3}{5})}{{s}^{2}+9}=-\\frac{1}{15(s+6)}+\\frac{s+9}{15({s}^{2}+9)}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+6}} & ={e}^{-6t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =-\\frac{1}{15}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+6}}+\\frac{1}{15}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}}+\\frac{1}{5}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}} \\\\ y(t) & =-\\frac{1}{15}{e}^{-6t}+\\frac{1}{15}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06fedec8-5aed-52f9-bd4f-aa81b9180ad4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems With Sinusoidal Forcing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8baa5b61-c7f4-5e80-aee7-ae3a3c42e6a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376406} {:answer/id #uuid "7b4df670-1338-5cb9-b2b0-168e2a7ae20d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+2}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376407} {:answer/id #uuid "1270d2c0-c184-5c8e-9f73-d07a611a2929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376408} {:answer/id #uuid "299071b0-6cd4-5827-af71-3e4ac395f4b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376409} {:answer/id #uuid "465592ec-05fb-5eea-b342-3868141a3e41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}+s+2}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1270d2c0-c184-5c8e-9f73-d07a611a2929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376408} :answer-field/id #uuid "990af204-11dc-5a5d-8d13-56d46c1b808f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376405} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fd4f90c-f140-5ba5-87ac-566fcbfef070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376412} {:answer/id #uuid "86b0153e-3fef-584e-b35f-4d76999a7c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376413} {:answer/id #uuid "807655a7-ff0e-5cb5-ba4a-1d9c942ddbd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376414} {:answer/id #uuid "585cb1fb-6dee-53e3-9b39-cba8c9d8953d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "585cb1fb-6dee-53e3-9b39-cba8c9d8953d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376415} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd70f12e-ec64-5657-b4c6-7155a1c48128" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376411} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d55f8187-e81d-5c10-94c8-e29021bc7885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376417} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea966a6-da44-5574-90bb-a2c3a3ff14e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-t}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376418} {:answer/id #uuid "2b9f6e58-9388-534f-bd3f-def7f32d3ad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376419} {:answer/id #uuid "368419f5-3c94-5ab9-9f6b-3be5a0d87e74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "368419f5-3c94-5ab9-9f6b-3be5a0d87e74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376420} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e7fa98f-2bdb-5d90-a00b-fb1963ffa565" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376416}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f44dbcab-4002-5eb8-9303-ab06ab01d7f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-343057" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+L{y}=L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-2)+Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s)-2 & =\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, add $2$ to the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+1)Y(s) & =2+\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}+1)}{{s}^{2}+1}+\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+1)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+1),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}=\\frac{A}{s+1}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n2{s}^{2}+s+3=A({s}^{2}+1)+(Bs+C)(s+1)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-1,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n2(-1)^{2}+(-1)+3=A((-1)^{2}+1)+0\\,⟹\\,4=2A\\,⟹\\,A=2.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n2=A+B\\,⟹\\,2=2+B\\,⟹\\,B=0.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n3=A+C\\,⟹\\,3=2+C\\,⟹\\,C=1.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} & ={e}^{-t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} \\\\ y(t) & =2{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06fedec8-5aed-52f9-bd4f-aa81b9180ad4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems With Sinusoidal Forcing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5b6ff33-b3c5-5e46-a551-22cd66674443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376423} {:answer/id #uuid "659dae4a-45bd-52d8-8396-c265d99c0563" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-2}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376424} {:answer/id #uuid "77612b3a-8002-505a-83a9-e88405f9af63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376425} {:answer/id #uuid "821d3293-cec8-5424-936a-77a38f82223c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376426} {:answer/id #uuid "8ecf2500-b0bf-5cb2-972a-cffd3da8acf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-2{s}^{2}+3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "821d3293-cec8-5424-936a-77a38f82223c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376426} :answer-field/id #uuid "db84eb9e-aae1-562d-b035-593874dc9934" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376422} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c27890d-c0eb-5351-b299-f9ed9d4631ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s+3}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376429} {:answer/id #uuid "af0f4937-6ad1-5cf0-a9aa-f660ea241834" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+3}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376430} {:answer/id #uuid "faf6eaf8-d467-5ca6-b6cc-ddf872d10da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s+3}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376431} {:answer/id #uuid "9f0582a8-41d8-5b71-8ff4-15a31d787c29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{s+3}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c27890d-c0eb-5351-b299-f9ed9d4631ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s+3}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376429} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9466f2c-8e0d-55c6-92e8-36aeaddfcbc5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376428} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be2ac929-bdad-5d8d-9c2d-68dad3336e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376434} {:answer/id #uuid "b004108b-23f4-5a63-b752-f4475b205710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376435} {:answer/id #uuid "b52b8c1a-2149-5e3c-bddb-930baf24f1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376436} {:answer/id #uuid "9e22ad16-56d2-5b2b-8d30-fb1f7f3284de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{-3t}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be2ac929-bdad-5d8d-9c2d-68dad3336e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376434} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b341a77-30d1-5a15-929c-9c7272dec395" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba6ac491-3a92-5a80-bc18-d0291dfbd502" :question/math-academy-id "q-343063" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+3y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+3L{y}=2L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}-3L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-(-2))+3Y(s) & =2(\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4})-3(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}) \\\\ (s+3)Y(s)+2 & =\\frac{4-3s}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, subtract $2$ from the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{4-3s}{{s}^{2}+4}-2 \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{4-3s}{{s}^{2}+4}-\\frac{2({s}^{2}+4)}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+3)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+4),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}=\\frac{A}{s+3}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+4}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n-2{s}^{2}-3s-4=A({s}^{2}+4)+(Bs+C)(s+3)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-3,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n-2(-3)^{2}-3(-3)-4=A((-3)^{2}+4)+0\\,⟹\\,-13=13A\\,⟹\\,A=-1.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n-2=A+B\\,⟹\\,-2=-1+B\\,⟹\\,B=-1.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n-4=4A+3C\\,⟹\\,-4=4(-1)+3C\\,⟹\\,C=0.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=-\\frac{1}{s+3}+\\frac{-s}{{s}^{2}+4}=-\\frac{1}{s+3}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} & ={e}^{-3t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\ y(t) & =-{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376438 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1417a42-f47a-5611-84be-f331c75287a9" :knowledge-point/title "Laplace Transforms of First-Order Linear IVPs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c2bd063-1dbf-58df-afb5-388fe0385026" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+8s+15}{3s(s-1)(s-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376440} {:answer/id #uuid "cae2b1cb-de48-5392-ae95-6dbb3e35566c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+15}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376441} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3bd02a-ea68-50d4-be82-2b6a73294919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+12}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376442} {:answer/id #uuid "c4da58da-5cc5-5ced-81cf-3a41be481c6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+8s+12}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376443} {:answer/id #uuid "d07c0b75-bb23-52b6-b96f-30d1a9a2e8bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+15}{3s(s+1)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cae2b1cb-de48-5392-ae95-6dbb3e35566c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+15}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376441} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c11fea9-f8dc-53c5-853b-3d0025d40343" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f1155af6-d35d-51d3-b6a5-6b676a893cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-343110" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>2$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-2y=5-2{e}^{-t},\\,y(0)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}-2y} & =L{5-2{e}^{-t}} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =5L{1}-2L{{e}^{-t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=\\frac{1}{3}:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)=sY(s)-\\frac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{n}} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0} \\\\ L{{e}^{at}} & =\\frac{1}{s-a},\\,s>a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ L{{e}^{-t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-(-1)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =5L{1}-2L{{e}^{-t}} \\\\ (sY(s)-\\frac{1}{3})-2Y(s) & =\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{2}{s+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{2}{s+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{s(s+1)+15(s+1)-6s}{3s(s+1)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+15}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1417a42-f47a-5611-84be-f331c75287a9" :knowledge-point/title "Laplace Transforms of First-Order Linear IVPs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da631c34-f90b-51ac-916a-1e7ff25bfae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{2}(s+4)},\\,s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376447} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9fce76-5d04-56f9-b58b-5175843b85e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s-3}{s+4},\\,s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376448} {:answer/id #uuid "534be448-b414-51cd-a75e-f898be084991" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{5{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{3}(s+4)},\\,s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376449} {:answer/id #uuid "17fd459e-9408-5baa-b98d-d135c26ab358" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{3{s}^{2}+2s+1}{{s}^{2}(s+4)},\\,s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376450} {:answer/id #uuid "90044f58-b7b7-522b-85ce-818154fcc86e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}+1}{s(s+4)},\\,s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17fd459e-9408-5baa-b98d-d135c26ab358" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{3{s}^{2}+2s+1}{{s}^{2}(s+4)},\\,s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376450} :answer-field/id #uuid "45c89ceb-0a77-5232-8f9f-727cb0c5e5b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7d5c1cef-5ffa-52dc-89d4-1aa20679c3f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-64480" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>0$ if\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4y=2+t,\\,y(0)=3.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}+4y} & =L{2+t} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}+4L{y} & =2L{1}+L{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=3:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)=sY(s)-3\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ L{t} & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}+4L{y} & =2L{1}+L{t} \\\\ (sY(s)-3)+4Y(s) & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ sY(s)+4Y(s) & =3+\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ (s+4)Y(s) & =\\frac{3{s}^{2}+2s+1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{3{s}^{2}+2s+1}{{s}^{2}(s+4)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1417a42-f47a-5611-84be-f331c75287a9" :knowledge-point/title "Laplace Transforms of First-Order Linear IVPs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28957ba5-c113-5005-a547-95c52aab98bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{4s+1}{2{s}^{3}(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376454} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf00a22-6595-513b-a712-3b6539f99041" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-2}{{s}^{3}(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376455} {:answer/id #uuid "080aad2f-0a38-52fa-9cc6-190d356821c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{3}(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376456} {:answer/id #uuid "26b06a91-be56-5f1f-91c0-226da90a3878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{4{s}^{2}+1}{4s(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376457} {:answer/id #uuid "4a536516-694a-58cf-bde1-43abb8d8d33a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "080aad2f-0a38-52fa-9cc6-190d356821c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{3}(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376456} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d2df3f1-109f-5092-9d75-68ae8e81af3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d18fffc1-68fb-5dfb-a521-2a4ffbf9bc9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-64482" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>0$ if\n\n$$\n2{y}^{′}+2y=4+{t}^{2},\\,y(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{2{y}^{′}+2y} & =L{4+{t}^{2}} \\\\ 2L{{y}^{′}}+2L{y} & =4L{1}+L{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)=sY(s)\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ L{{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2L{{y}^{′}}+2L{y} & =4L{1}+L{{t}^{2}} \\\\ 2sY(s)+2Y(s) & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ (2s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}+2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2(2{s}^{2}+1)}{{s}^{3}(2s+2)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{3}(s+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
